OL,3,GNEWSALive facial recognition to be
OL,4,Aintroduced in city
OL,5,
OL,6,FLive facial recognition (LFR)
OL,7,Ftechnology will be introduced in a city
OL,8,Fas part of a police force's efforts to
OL,9,Fprevent crime, protect the public and
OL,10,Fsafeguard vulnerable people.
OL,12,FAvon and Somerset Police said the LFR
OL,13,Ftechnology will be overt and clearly
OL,14,Fsignposted when it is rolled out in
OL,15,FBath on 25 November.
OL,17,FLFR uses CCTV cameras to help police
OL,18,Fidentify people in crowded spaces who
OL,19,Fare on pre-authorised watchlists. All
OL,20,Fcaptured images that do not match
OL,21,Fsomeone on the watchlist are
OL,22,Fautomatically and permanently deleted.
OL,23,APub: 05-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
